@* 
    Prevents a click from being silently swallowed before the page is live.

    Interactive server components are pre-rendered as ordinary HTML first, and their event handlers do
    not exist until the circuit connects. A button in that window looks completely normal and does
    nothing when pressed. On a screen whose buttons submit and approve invoices, a click that appears
    to work and does not is unacceptable, so the controls are visibly held until the page can act on
    them. The data attribute is also what the browser tests wait on, which keeps them honest: they
    cannot pass by clicking something a real user could not have used either.
*@
<div class="action-gate @(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "is-live" : "is-connecting")"
     data-interactive="@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "true" : "false")">
    @ChildContent

    @if (!RendererInfo.IsInteractive)
    {
        <p class="small muted" role="status">Connecting — these actions become available in a moment.</p>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
